# Build-context hygiene for the backend image (DOCKER-PR1-01, REQ-DOCKER-009).
#
# Keeps the context lean AND prevents test/ artifacts from leaking into the
# builder/runtime images. The REQ-009 "infra-only diff" guard is not polluted
# by copying test/ or node_modules into layers.
#
# Load-bearing paths are NOT excluded (must reach the build):
#   - prisma/            (postinstall prisma generate reads schema.prisma;
#                         migrate service runs `prisma migrate deploy`)
#   - scripts/           (C1 — seed service runs scripts/seed-with-guard.sh)
#   - src/               (nest build → dist/)
#   - package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, tsconfig*.json,
#     nest-cli.json

node_modules
dist
coverage

# Env files never belong in an image.
.env
.env.*

# Test artifacts are host-side concerns; excluding them shrinks the context and
# guarantees test/ code can never ship inside a serving image.
test/fixtures
test/e2e
test/docker

# Docs + VCS noise.
*.md
.git
.gitignore

# Local editor / OS cruft.
.DS_Store
*.log
